# Malaga Book Club Bot

Async Telegram bot (portfolio: layered architecture, async-first, strict typing). Operator docs: `README.md`. Full map: `CONTEXT.md`.

## Stack

- Python 3.12+, `mypy`, `ruff`
- aiogram 3.x, PostgreSQL 16, SQLAlchemy 2.0 + `asyncpg`, Alembic (async)
- Pydantic v2, `pydantic-settings`, `httpx`, APScheduler
- Docker Compose: Postgres `5432` (`book_club_db`) + bot (`book_club_bot`)

## Layers

Handlers → Services → Repositories → Models

- `app/bot/handlers/` — `base`, `books` (DM `/suggest`), `clubs`, `group_suggest`, `group_card_review`, `club_setup`, `cycle_open`, `meeting`, `admin` (schedule days)
- `app/bot/middlewares/` — `DbSessionMiddleware` injects `AsyncSession`
- `app/bot/club_publish.py` — announcements, polls, calendar invite
- `app/services/` — catalog, cycle, destination, `club_scheduler`, meeting invite
- `app/db/models.py` — `User` (`active_club_id`), `Book`, `ClubSettings` (one row per group), `SuggestionCycle` (per club), `Suggestion`, `PendingGroupCard`, `VotePoll`, `MeetingPoll`, `MeetingTimePoll` (+ unused `Meeting`/`Vote`/`RSVP`)
- `main.py` — polling + FSM `MemoryStorage` + scheduler

## Status

- Alembic: initial tables → suggestion cycles → suggest topic → vote/meeting polls + winner fields → pending group cards → multi-club → meeting time polls
- Cycle: open next month → hashtag in group (admin review before poll) or `/suggest` in DM → `/start_vote` → `/close_vote` (runoff on tie; meeting-date poll on a single winner) → `/close_meeting_poll` → optional `/start_meeting_time_poll` (weekends) → `/create_meeting` (`.ics`; date/time can be typed if there was no poll)
- `/reset_vote` republishes book polls from suggestions since the 1st of the collection month without wiping the cycle
- Scheduler opens suggestions and starts book polls per bound club (pauses if group cards await review); it does not close them
- DM uses one active group; `/clubs` is hidden and only needed when a user is in several bound chats
- `DEBUG=true` allows reopening the same month
